### Summary
Calculate the sum of the elements on the primary and secondary diagonals of a square matrix, excluding any overlapping elements.

### Description
1. Given a square matrix `mat`.
2. Compute the sum of all elements on both the primary diagonal (from top-left to bottom-right) and the secondary diagonal (from top-right to bottom-left).
3. Exclude any elements that are part of both diagonals.

### I/O
- [mat = [[1,2,3],[4,5,6],[7,8,9]]] => 25

### Algo/Datastructure
- Algorithm: Iterative Diagonal Sum Calculation

### Code
```javascript
const diagonalSum = mat => {
  let sum = 0;
  let j = mat[0].length - 1;

  for (let i = 0; i < mat.length; i++, j--) {
    if (i !== j) sum += mat[i][j];
    sum += mat[i][i];
  }

  return sum;
};
```

